<title>REPUBLIC OF IRELAND: Tuskar shareholders approve reverse takeover.</title>
<headline>Tuskar shareholders approve reverse takeover.</headline>
<dateline>DUBLIN 1996-10-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shareholders in Irish-based exploration company Tuskar Resources Plc approved its acquisition of a 40-percent interest in an oil mining lease off Nigeria at an extraordinary meeting on Friday.</p>
<p>The deal is effectively a reverse takeover which will lead to the Houston-based Allied/Camac group becoming a 65-percent shareholder in Tuskar's enlarged share capital, Tuskar said.</p>
<p>&quot;The acquisition of the 40-percent interest...and the effective reverse takeover of the company by Camac/Allied marks the beginning of the rebuilding and reshaping of the company's portfolio and growth strategy,&quot; Tuskar Chairman Duncan McGregor said in a statement.</p>
<p>-- Dublin Newsroom +353 1 660 3377</p>
</text>
